.TH AVR\-VM\-DELETE 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-delete \- Delete a VM.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm delete
[OPTIONS] CUSTOMER_VM_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a VM.
.PP
Delete a VM. Asynchronous while live: shows DELETING until the node confirms the stop.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fICUSTOMER_VM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the VM is fully deleted before returning.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
Seconds to wait when --wait is set. (default: 300)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the raw API response as JSON.
.SH SEE ALSO
